{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1217981-house-rule-alternative-to-conjunctional-arcana","id":1217981,"title":"House Rule: Alternative to Conjunctional Arcana","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-12T09:04:04-07:00","id":1217981,"title":"House Rule: Alternative to Conjunctional Arcana","content":"The new edition of Mage did a pretty good job of minimizing the number of spells that require conjunctional Arcana - a design philosophy I fully support. The previous edition could get genuinely silly with otherwise nifty spells that required access to just the right combination of Arcana, which often put them on a shelf that was out of reach of PCs who hadn't already decided to go that route. Nevertheless, there are still a few spells with conjunctional effects as little add-ons, and I'm finding quite a few people on the forums who say &quot;you can't do X with just Y-Arcanum; you also need Z-Arcanum.&quot; And those arguments can be pretty compelling. Turning a person into a statue *doesn't* feel entirely within he purview of Life alone, for example. But here's an alternative I've used at my table:<br /> <br /> Whenever a spell calls for a conjunctional Arcanum, consider access to that Arcanum an *alternative* to a Reach effect. If the effect requires conjunctional Forces 1, for example, you can either get that effect by having Forces 1 or by adding +1 Reach. This gets a little bit more ad hoc-ish when you're talking about conjunctional effects that require three or four dots in another Arcanum. I generally add Reach equal to half the number of dots required in the conjunctional Arcanum. So if you want to use Life to turn an enemy to stone, you can do that as a +2 Reach effect. I'll drop that down if the effect is, in my opinion, more of a matter of flavor than something that grants a mechanical benefit. The Matter 4 &quot;subject's gear changes to fit her new form&quot; effect? Probably only a +1 Reach effect.<br /> <br /> The in-game justification might be that all magic, all Arcana, are ultimately connected. They overlap in a thousand tiny ways, any one of which could be the subject of some mage's Obsession. After all, every Supernal Realm contains all the Arcana - just in varying amounts. So a mage can push an Arcanum out of its natural channels to accomplish things that seem like they should require a conjunctional Arcanum - albeit at an increased risk of Paradox.<br /> <br /> Just something I thought I'd share while taking a break from the current writing assignment. Okay. Back at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T18:39:03-07:00","id":1220387,"title":"","content":"Hmm... this may even work as a set of Arcana Attainments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T21:22:43-07:00","id":1220429,"title":"","content":"That house rule would generate some frankly ludicrous results when combined with a Demesne.<br /> Also couldn't Mages just add a massive amount of conjunctive Arcana, then contain and scour the resultant Condition.<br /> One Lethal for smashing the boundaries of the Arcana into little pieces, and getting all the Reach effects you like.<br /> <br /> Probably best to add a cap to the amount of Reach's worth of conjunctive Arcana you can draw upon with that method.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T22:45:06-07:00","id":1220440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1217981-house-rule-alternative-to-conjunctional-arcana?p=1220429#post1220429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also couldn't Mages just add a massive amount of conjunctive Arcana, then contain and scour the resultant Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Condition has to time out first and there's only so much the Wisdom roll can do to mitigate how bad the Condition can get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T23:25:19-07:00","id":1220450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1217981-house-rule-alternative-to-conjunctional-arcana?p=1220440#post1220440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Condition has to time out first and there's only so much the Wisdom roll can do to mitigate how bad the Condition can get.</div> </div> </div> </div>Until errata removes all the 'the mage Scours the Condition from her Pattern' resolution options from all the example conditions, and clarifies that as not being a method by which the issue can be resolved. I'm unconvinced.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T00:58:36-07:00","id":1220460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1217981-house-rule-alternative-to-conjunctional-arcana?p=1220450#post1220450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Until errata removes all the 'the mage Scours the Condition from her Pattern' resolution options from all the example conditions, and clarifies that as not being a method by which the issue can be resolved. I'm unconvinced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn\u2019t Scouring become an option only after the Conditions\u2019 time lapse?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T01:30:33-07:00","id":1220463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1217981-house-rule-alternative-to-conjunctional-arcana?p=1220460#post1220460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn\u2019t Scouring become an option only after the Conditions\u2019 time lapse?</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules do not state so, it mentions it becomes the 'only' option to cure the Abyssal taint, once the Condition has lapsed.<br /> <br /> Which combined with the mention of Scouring in the Conditions section as a possible resolution, and the fact that the Condition auto-resolves the moment it lapses, suggests you can still Scour it prior to that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T02:37:11-07:00","id":1220476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1217981-house-rule-alternative-to-conjunctional-arcana?p=1220463#post1220463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The rules do not state so, it mentions it becomes the 'only' option to cure the Abyssal taint, once the Condition has lapsed.<br /> <br /> Which combined with the mention of Scouring in the Conditions section as a possible resolution, and the fact that the Condition auto-resolves the moment it lapses, suggests you can still Scour it prior to that point.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm, good point. Though thematically, Paradox Conditions working differently make sense as well. Decisions, decisions...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T04:52:39-07:00","id":1220503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1217981-house-rule-alternative-to-conjunctional-arcana?p=1220450#post1220450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Until errata removes all the 'the mage Scours the Condition from her Pattern' resolution options from all the example conditions, and clarifies that as not being a method by which the issue can be resolved. I'm unconvinced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Outside of the context of the Condition writeup structure itself, all the framing of how Scouring works combined with the fact that not having to let it lapse first defeats the point of there being a variable timer for it to lapse in the first place indicates that the intent is not for the practical outcome of Paradox Conditions to be that you take a point of resistant lethal damage on top of however much resistant bashing damage you took to mitigate it in the first place. There's not going to be a second run of errata to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T05:14:46-07:00","id":1220513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1217981-house-rule-alternative-to-conjunctional-arcana?p=1220503#post1220503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's not going to be a second run of errata to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>An FAQ could clear things up though!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T06:56:08-07:00","id":1220533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1217981-house-rule-alternative-to-conjunctional-arcana?p=1220513#post1220513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An FAQ could clear things up though!</div> </div> </div> </div>Please stop trying to provoke that argument again, you\u2019re not getting a FAQ.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T07:28:31-07:00","id":1220535,"title":"","content":"Based on the fact that clearing the Condition is described as &quot;Scouring&quot; and that that word has a specific mechanical meaning (p. 87), I'm not so sure that &quot;take a Paradox Condition and then Scour it away&quot; is such a large loophole. First, the lethal damage inflicted by Scouring is resistant, so it takes two days to recover from resolving a Paradox Condition that way. Second, Scouring can only be done once per day if your Gnosis is less than 5 (and slightly more than that at higher Gnosis), so you can only clear a Paradox Condition once (or perhaps a couple of times) per day - and at the expense of using Scouring to replenish your Mana. In this case, Scouring to resolve a Paradox Condition is more limited than for restoring Mana, since it must deal lethal damage rather than giving you the option of reducing an Attribute.<br /> <br /> I recognize that the Paradox Condition section doesn't explicitly say &quot;resistant lethal damage.&quot; I'm less surprised that it doesn't explicitly link one form of Scouring with the other, since that would have taken significantly more words than adding &quot;resistant.&quot; And I really have no counterargument to Demesne other than to say that anything that eliminates Paradox risk is going to be abused by someone.<br /> <br /> As with any system, intent matters, but sometimes it doesn't get spelled out enough, which results in objections on forums and abuse at the table. The intent of this house rule isn't to let everyone add some Reach to do anything they want with any spell in any Arcanum. It's meant to address the moment at the table when a player says &quot;I want to do X thing that I think fits the Arcana I have,&quot; but the Storyteller strokes his beard thoughtfully and says &quot;that's flavorful, but it feels like it should also require conjunctional Arcanum Y, which you don't have,&quot; at which point the player sags in her chair a bit at having been prevented from casting the spell she wants (or else play grinds to a halt as the troupe debates whether it should or shouldn't require Arcanum Y). This approach instead encourages the Storyteller to say yes - or at least &quot;that probably also requires an Apprentice's understanding of Acranum Y, so if you don't have Arcanum Y, add +1 Reach.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd say that especially for big conjunctional effects it's fair to say that achieving them by adding Reach doesn't quite have the gracefulness of the original. If you add +3 Reach to the Create Life spell to give your creation a mind (instead of having Mind 5), for example, you have absolutely no control over the resultant personality of that mind - only an assurance that your creation will have a real working brain that does...something and wants...some other things.<br /> <br /> (And honestly, I'd probably just let that be the case without needing to add Reach at all. You can create perfect strangers from thin air who have no inherent loyalty to you and might, on the contrary, become your enemies? Oo, how broken! Dude, unless we're on a deserted island, an Apprentice of Fate can pretty much achieve the same result, and at least she has assurances that the stranger has skills or connections that are actually useful to her right now. I can see that how that could cause a problem at someone else's table, just not mine.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T15:03:05-07:00","id":1220631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1217981-house-rule-alternative-to-conjunctional-arcana?p=1220535#post1220535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on the fact that clearing the Condition is described as &quot;Scouring&quot; and that that word has a specific mechanical meaning (p. 87), I'm not so sure that &quot;take a Paradox Condition and then Scour it away&quot; is such a large loophole.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not so much the idea that it's a loophole as it is the fact that it's the only resolution method that isn't mentioned in the Paradox Conditions writeup's &quot;there are two resolution mechanics for a Paradox Condition&quot; blurb and the individual Paradox Condition blurbs already have the time-out listed as a regular resolution mechanic in addition to the Arcane Beat criterion despite &quot;the Condition lapses&quot; being repeated contrasted with &quot;the Condition resolves,&quot; the general Condition notes outright saying &quot;don't take a Beat for just waiting out a Condition with a natural time-limit,&quot; and Scouring the effect from your Pattern otherwise only being brought up in the context of your only recourse when the lapse has let the Abyss into your Pattern.<br /> <br /> The contradiction in presented mechanics is clearly present, but one of them makes more sense than the other when placed in the context of the thematic space high-Wisdom and low-Wisdom characters ostensibly occupy; is it more likely that a character who seldom casts magic frivolously or without concern for bystanders suffers through a month of unmitigatable magical fallout in search of the escape clause, or does retreating for two days to recover from cutting the corruption out of their soul make more sense for that archetype than the one that can't keep casual acquaintances from getting entangled in magical shenanigans without a Shadow Name?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T20:40:56-07:00","id":1220703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1217981-house-rule-alternative-to-conjunctional-arcana?p=1220631#post1220631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not so much the idea that it's a loophole as it is the fact that it's the only resolution method that isn't mentioned in the Paradox Conditions writeup's &quot;there are two resolution mechanics for a Paradox Condition&quot; blurb and the individual Paradox Condition blurbs already have the time-out listed as a regular resolution mechanic in addition to the Arcane Beat criterion despite &quot;the Condition lapses&quot; being repeated contrasted with &quot;the Condition resolves,&quot; the general Condition notes outright saying &quot;don't take a Beat for just waiting out a Condition with a natural time-limit,&quot; and Scouring the effect from your Pattern otherwise only being brought up in the context of your only recourse when the lapse has let the Abyss into your Pattern.<br /> <br /> The contradiction in presented mechanics is clearly present, but one of them makes more sense than the other when placed in the context of the thematic space high-Wisdom and low-Wisdom characters ostensibly occupy; is it more likely that a character who seldom casts magic frivolously or without concern for bystanders suffers through a month of unmitigatable magical fallout in search of the escape clause, or does retreating for two days to recover from cutting the corruption out of their soul make more sense for that archetype than the one that can't keep casual acquaintances from getting entangled in magical shenanigans without a Shadow Name?</div> </div> </div> </div>I see your point regarding Paradox Conditions. I haven't read these in a couple years, and I'm having a little trouble remembering the rationale for the mechanics. As I recall, I *think* the idea was that high Wisdom characters had longer to resolve the Condition because Scouring it away after it lapsed was even worse. If that's the case, I'm not sure the mechanics achieve that. I'd much rather take a level of resistant lethal damage than have an Abyssal entity use me to Manifest. I mean, the delay does give you more time to make the decision of whether you need to Scour and be done with it or whether seeking out the regular Resolution condition is a better solution. But I don't remember that being part of the discussion. The &quot;two ways&quot; language is an artifact of an earlier draft, as the idea of Scouring prior to letting the Condition lapse came a little later in the process; originally, it was the &quot;you done f'd up&quot; penalty for letting the Condition lapse instead of resolving it.<br /> <br /> Weirdly, I think it might do a better job punishing low-Wisdom mages if there is initially a generalized Paradox Condition that does nothing except put a countdown timer on you and give you a detectable Abyssal taint. You can Scour away that timer whenever you want by suffering the resistant lethal damage. If you wait until it lapses, it converts to a specific Paradox Condition that works the way the as-written Paradox Conditions work, except once the &quot;harmless&quot; Paradox Condition turns into one with teeth, you no longer have the option of Scouring it away. You *have* to clear it by being used to let an Abyssal entity manifest, successfully casting a spell without suffering a Paradox while laboring under a bunch of extra Paradox dice, or whatever. Of course, &quot;punishment&quot; is relative, since resolving a Paradox Condition earns a beat (two beats if you let the &quot;harmless&quot; timer Condition award a beat when it is Scoured or converts), while Scouring it away does not (or only earns one if Scouring it or letting it lapse still awards a beat). But a high-Wisdom mage - even one with six or seven Paradox timers - can reasonably Scour away all of it without dropping into wound penalties by simply limiting his use of risky magic. The low-Wisdom mage, on the other hand, is going to be buried in Swords of Damocles unless he accepts serious injuries to dodge a few of those nasty &quot;screws you until you resolve it&quot; Conditions.<br /> <br /> All of that assumes that the timer Condition explicitly violates the &quot;only one version of the same Condition can affect a character at any given time&quot; rule and also assumes that Scouring away timer Conditions can be done more than the usual once per day (slightly higher for Gnosis 5+). Alternatively, the point of the timer Condition is that it essentially inoculates you against gaining a timer Condition until you either Scour it away or the timer runs out. High-Wisdom mages won't be forced to Scour more often than once per month, while low-Wisdom mages pretty much need to decide within an hour whether to Scour or lapse, and they don't have the option to Scour if they've already reached their Scouring limit for the day. A medium-Wisdom mage always has the choice to either Scour or lapse, but they can't sit pretty for a few weeks, utterly immune to further Abyssal corruption, the way a high-Wisdom mage can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T21:50:38-07:00","id":1220719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1217981-house-rule-alternative-to-conjunctional-arcana?p=1220703#post1220703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see your point regarding Paradox Conditions. I haven't read these in a couple years, and I'm having a little trouble remembering the rationale for the mechanics. As I recall, I *think* the idea was that high Wisdom characters had longer to resolve the Condition because Scouring it away after it lapsed was even worse. If that's the case, I'm not sure the mechanics achieve that. I'd much rather take a level of resistant lethal damage than have an Abyssal entity use me to Manifest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, in that specific case the Abyssal entity is getting all of a scene's activity out of the deal due to the act of Manifestation chopping the legs out from under it, and it benefits the portrayal of the slow slide down the Wisdom scale to emphasize that Abyssal entities are more &quot;bugs in the code of reality&quot; than &quot;actively malevolent forces that are out to specifically hurt you in particular.&quot;<br /> <br /> Resistant lethal damage from Scouring Paradoxes out of your Pattern seems to fill approximately the same role as regular damage does in Vampire or severe Clarity damage does in Changeling \u2014 it's a point of attrition that makes it that much harder to deal with sustained problems without taking time off to patch yourself up, but there's a reason it's seldom a long-term problem for downtime-typical states of affairs on its own instead of a story-building complication in its own right the way the normal Resolution mechanics are.<br /> <br /> The general framework of 2e seems much more geared towards &quot;Paradox is going to happen with some frequency in a typical area and it's not even going to be a big deal most of the time; that's how it gets you&quot; than &quot;Paradox is a constant and immediate threat to the Awakened at a personal level&quot; \u2014 it appears to be foundational to the shape of the Mana economy in a more lasting sense than how much you can get out of mortification of the flesh.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Weirdly, I think it might do a better job punishing low-Wisdom mages if there is initially a generalized Paradox Condition that does nothing except put a countdown timer on you and give you a detectable Abyssal taint. </div> </div> </div>Where this falls apart is that containing a Paradox is an entirely voluntary process, and it's one that low-Wisdom mages are directly discouraged from by both the mechanics and the thematic space they inhabit \u2014 the penalty releasing a Paradox imposes on the casting roll does nothing to prevent you from simply trying again, and spending Mana to reduce your Paradox dice is method-agnostic besides, to say nothing of how the observed ability to use a suitable Demesne to outright negate the risk with plain old privacy works as well for the disconnected amoral wizard as it does for the enlightened hermit-sage.<br /> <br /> Pretty much the only reason low-Wisdom mages have to contain a Paradox is because it eliminates the prospect of a spellcasting penalty altogether regardless of the outcome and they don't have the time to spare on retries; this is the same line of thought that makes Blood Sacrifice an attractive option in the sort of feedback loops that can make a Mad One, and I feel like that kind of focus is also pretty on-brand for a character that stands a chance of regularly spawning long-lasting glitches in the mythic underpinnings of the word in the pursuit of esoteric knowledge and/or power unless they occasionally bleed the extra excuse to burn more Mana out of their system.<br /> <br /> I'm rambling a bit here (long day and all that), but between the lack of much in the way of strong evidence in the fiction for &quot;Pattern Scouring is the main way mages get their Mana and losing an opportunity to do so is the primary downside of cutting a Paradox Condition out of your existence&quot; (besides &quot;Scouring gives you three Mana and that's a pretty big amount&quot;) and Scouring being both easier and less interesting to deal with than the risks mandated by normal Resolution criteria (when the entire point of Conditions is to feed into character advancement by rewarding engagement with narrative complications), I can't really get behind &quot;Individuated Paradox Conditions can be carved out of a character by an act of will at any time without regard for their Wisdom&quot; even if it weren't regularly put forth by people as a way in which the Paradox mechanics are supposedly toothless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T20:06:36-07:00","id":1221051,"title":"","content":"@Satchel: No worries about rambling. I've been doing plenty of it in this thread - starting with the OP, which was written as a bit of a break from more structured writing time. My group, um, playtested things way too early, modified lots to taste, played for a year or so until the final game came out, and then, rather than adopting the official rules, incorporated the new stuff into an already heinously homebrewed system. So while I was involved in writing Mage, my experience running it...doesn't always line up with everyone else's, so sometimes I forget how a few of the official systems work. Paradox Conditions is one of those, so if I seem like I'm spitballing a bit (possibly with a side of making assumptions based on an interpretation of the rules that doesn't wholly match RAW), it's because I probably am.<br /> <br /> I wasn't so much running &quot;The Fallen World Chronicle&quot; as &quot;The Abyss Encroaches Chronicle&quot; - much more elaborate rules for containing versus controlling (i.e. releasing or not containing) Paradox and systems for dealing with the resulting Abyssal taint. Like, for example, controlling a Paradox pitted your spellcasting pool against the Paradox dice (rather than penalizing your roll). If you won the contest, there was zero negative consequence for casting a spell that way (unless the Paradox dice achieved an exceptional success, but even then the spell itself remained under your control). If the Paradox tied or won the contest, the spell became a Havoc (usually a Lesser Havoc, but rarely a Greater Havoc). Failure on the spellcasting roll with successes on the Paradox roll netted you Abyssal taint, which made Anomalies and Manifestations possible if it rose to certain thresholds. Abyssal taint bled off at the rate of one per day, but it was otherwise notoriously difficult to get rid of, and the Paradox Condition it imposed (each mage only ever had one, which flared up whenever he had more than a couple points of Abyssal taint) was worse the more taint you had accumulated and the higher your Gnosis.<br /> <br /> The idea behind controlling Paradox was to encourage players to participate in their characters' hubris by doing the math. &quot;Hm, if I add X Reach, that gives me a 2-die Paradox pool against my 6-die Gnosis + Arcanum, so the odds of something going wrong are negligible...&quot; Generate enough random results, however, and you'll eventually see something statistically improbable happen... But all of the math behind that contested roll was supported by the math of heavily modified spellcasting mechanics, which were significantly colored by specialized Merits, which relied on a significant change to how Arcane vs. regular Experiences could be spent... And so on and so forth and turtles all the way down. So 95% of my existing homebrew systems for Mage are completely meaningless away from my table.<br /> <br /> Okay, one more totally random detail: Sleeper witnesses didn't increase the risk of Paradox, and Dissonance wasn't a thing. However, any Anomaly generated by a Paradox? It always went after any Sleeper witnesses, first. If you had at least five Abyssal taint, that very likely meant an innocent bystander was killed or permanently transformed as a side-effect of your spell. Even if you had no taint before making that particular mistake, a random Sleeper would probably end up with some significant trauma in the form of a breaking point and some form of unpleasant, if temporary, condition. Killing someone accidentally with your magic does what to your Wisdom again? Oo. Ouch...<br /> <br /> Anyway, Reach as an alternative to a conjunctional Arcanum is about as readily shareable a system as I've got.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}